@title Famicom Mini - Hikari Shinwa - Palutena no Kagame (Japan)
@file Famicom Mini - Vol. 24 - Hikari Shinwa - Palutena no Kagame (J).gba
@game FPTJ
@chip EEPROM 64Kbit
@frozen dingbat-bios,mgba,nba
@save skip: registering a name writes nothing; the first save is at GAME OVER > セーブ スル, and the game-over screen never leaves "ヤラレチャッタ" in dingbat or the second reference (the Disk System file lookup's walk through unmapped memory never ends there, as at Famicom Mini Metroid's boot: docs/playtest-bugs.md §100). The 8 KB EEPROM written here holds only the 8 bytes "TRAPR..." at 0xFF8, from the boot.

# The Disk System version. Title, START: the file screen (セレクトシテクダサイ),
# A, START on ナマエ トウロク, START picks the first slot, A A: "アア",
# SELECT three times to トウロク オワル, START: back on the file screen with
# アア. START plays it: stage 1-1, four arrows, a step right, four more, the
# L+R menu (つづける / リセット / スリープモード), A back, then stand still
# until the shemum snakes take Pit's health (f~3400): "ヤラレチャッタ".
# Seen while authoring: from the menu on, mgba's enemies are a frame or so
# apart from dingbat-bios and the second reference (identical to each other
# throughout), and mgba's Pit dies earlier. At game_over mgba has gone on
# to コンティニュー スル / セーブ スル; dingbat-bios and the second reference
# stay on ヤラレチャッタ for good, START or not: the CPU sits in the walk
# loop (0x03003568-0x0300358C), lr far into unmapped memory, reading its
# own prefetched opcode 0x0A000005 rotated (0x050A0000). All three write
# the same 8 bytes at boot; mgba fills the rest of its file with 00,
# dingbat and the second reference with FF.
[new]
wait 300
checkpoint title window=30
press START
wait 120
checkpoint file_select window=30
press A
wait 60
press START
wait 60
press START
wait 40
press A
wait 24
press A
wait 24
checkpoint name_entry window=30
press SELECT
wait 24
press SELECT
wait 24
press SELECT
wait 24
press START
wait 40
checkpoint registered window=30
press START
wait 300
checkpoint stage1 window=30
tap B times=4 every=20 hold=6
hold RIGHT
wait 60
release
tap B times=4 every=20 hold=6
checkpoint play window=30
press L+R hold=10
wait 60
checkpoint menu window=30
press A
wait 60
checkpoint resumed window=30
wait 1500
checkpoint enemies window=30
wait 900
checkpoint game_over window=30

